      "research_entry": "Conditional finite protocol. Take a nonprincipal primitive Dirichlet character modulo q>1 and a uniformly translated starting phase s; measure the complex fluctuation chi(s+j), or use a primitive real quadratic character if real residuals are desired. Its covariance with the complex conjugate at shift h is c_q(h)/q. Hence m-step mean-square variance equals (1/q) sum_{e|q} mu(q/e) r_e(e-r_e), r_e=m mod e, and its full-period mean is J_2(q)/(6q). A rational finite convolution receiver is blind for every shift precisely when its polynomial contains Phi_q. Derive the sum with phase-dependent, multiple and nonprimitive channels if needed, retaining the missing frequency components rather than applying independent noise.",
      "scope": "The taskbook expressly allows this condition or a missing-interface audit when upstream 00/04/06 are unreturned. Their status is recorded separately. No astronomical prediction, native law or physical period is implied. Wave30 studied a different mode-doubling comparison on the same parent. This is the strongest registered arithmetic candidate outside wave31 parents.",
